Notebook[{Cell["Cassani invariant and rotating heterotic comparison", 
   "Title"], Cell["Version-3 human notation guide (documentation only; no \
Input cell is changed). In the compact solution and verifier notebooks: \
x=r^2; q1,q2,q3 are the harmonic parameters mu1,mu2,mu3, not normalized \
conserved charges; jrot is the rotation parameter j; U1,U2,U3 are the \
electric corrections delta u_I; B1,B2,B3 are the gauge-covariant fibre \
corrections; Om is delta omega; Ft, Gr, and Sq are the temporal warp, radial \
warp, and squashing corrections; P and S are delta p and delta s, where \
X1=exp(2p/3-s), X2=exp(2p/3+s), and X3=exp(-4p/3). Physical quantities are \
Q_I=Pi mu_I/(4 G5) and J1=J2=Pi j/(4 G5). See the report section \
'Human-readable notation and result at a glance' for the full dictionary.", 
   "Text"], Cell["Exact source matching, Eq. (3.31), and the remaining \
field-map qualification", "Subtitle"], Cell["This standalone notebook \
verifies the algebraic matching ledger for the single lambda3 standard-Weyl \
STU invariant used by the BMPV calculation. The three lambda_I couplings are \
independent; no cyclic sum is required. For the heterotic gravitational and \
mixed-Chern--Simons sector the choice is lambda1=lambda2=0 and \
lambda3=alphaPrime/8.", "Text"], Cell["The full heterotic invariant differs \
from the single standard-Weyl invariant by two curvature-free \
vector-multiplet invariants. The exact rotating BPS identity below proves \
that their values and first variations vanish, so the two theories have the \
same first-order EOM source on the rotating two-derivative background. The \
complete corrected ten-to-five-dimensional field map remains conditional.", 
   "Text"], Cell["1. Rotating dressed-field identity", "Section"], 
  Cell[BoxData["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"]; $HistoryLength=0;"], "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData["hprod = h1 h2 h3;\nfTildeI = hprod^(-1/3) {-1, 0, \
1};\nfTildeJ = hprod^(-1/3) {0, -1, 1};\ndressedDifference = Simplify[fTildeI \
- fTildeJ];\nexpectedDifference = hprod^(-1/3) {-1, 1, \
0};\ndThetaCancellation = TrueQ[dressedDifference[[3]] === \
0];\ndressedIdentityPass = TrueQ[dressedDifference === \
expectedDifference];\n\n(* XI/XJ=HJ/HI, hence d log(XI/XJ)=-d log(HI)+d \
log(HJ).\n   With e0=hprod^(-1/3) Theta, this is\n     FtildeI-FtildeJ = d \
log(XI/XJ) wedge e0. *)\nscalarGradientCoefficients = {-1, \
1};\nbpsRelationPass = TrueQ[\n  Take[dressedDifference, 2] === hprod^(-1/3) \
scalarGradientCoefficients];\n\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- \
*)\ndressedChecks=<|\"DressedFieldIdentityExactInTheta\"->dressedIdentityPass\
,\"DThetaCancels\"->dThetaCancellation,\"LocalBPSRelation\"->bpsRelationPass|\
>; dressedChecks"], "Input"], Cell["Expected exact output:", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData["<|\"DressedFieldIdentityExactInTheta\" -> True, \
\"DThetaCancels\" -> True, \"LocalBPSRelation\" -> True|>"], "Output"], 
  Cell["For A^I=H_I^(-1) Theta and X^I=H^(1/3)/H_I, the dTheta term cancels \
in Ftilde^I-Ftilde^J. No form of Theta or of the rotation one-form is \
assumed, so the statement is exact in j.", "Text"], 
  Cell["2. Vector invariant and its first variation", "Section"], 
  Cell["In a five-dimensional orthonormal frame let K be the dressed \
field-strength difference and p=d log(X^I/X^J). The curvature-free invariant \
is V=(K^2)^2-4 K^4+4 K^2 p^2-16 (K^2)_ab p^a p^b-4(p^2)^2. The substitution \
K=plus or minus e0 wedge p must annihilate V and every first derivative with \
respect to K and p.", "Text"], Cell[BoxData["dim = 5;\neta = \
DiagonalMatrix[{-1, 1, 1, 1, 1}];\nfvars = Association@Flatten@Table[{aa, bb} \
->\n    Symbol[\"f\" <> ToString[aa] <> ToString[bb]],\n  {aa, 0, dim - 1}, \
{bb, aa + 1, dim - 1}];\np = Array[pp, dim, 0];\nfdd = ConstantArray[0, {dim, \
dim}];\nKeyValueMap[(fdd[[#1[[1]] + 1, #1[[2]] + 1]] = #2;\n    fdd[[#1[[2]] \
+ 1, #1[[1]] + 1]] = -#2) &, fvars];\nfuu = eta . fdd . eta;\nfdu = fdd . \
eta;\nf2 = Expand[Total[Flatten[fdd fuu]]];\nf4 = Expand[Tr[MatrixPower[fdu, \
4]]];\npup = eta . p;\np2 = Expand[p . pup];\nf2dd = Simplify[fdd . eta . \
Transpose[fdd]];\nf2pp = Expand[pup . f2dd . pup];\nvectorInvariant = \
Expand[\n  f2^2 - 4 f4 + 4 f2 p2 - 16 f2pp - 4 p2^2];\nbpsRules = \
Join[{p[[1]] -> 0},\n  Table[fvars[{0, ii}] -> p[[ii + 1]], {ii, 1, dim - \
1}],\n  Flatten@Table[fvars[{ii, jj}] -> 0,\n    {ii, 1, dim - 1}, {jj, ii + \
1, dim - 1}]];\nvectorValue = Factor[vectorInvariant /. \
bpsRules];\nvectorGradientF = Factor[(D[vectorInvariant, #] /. bpsRules)] & \
/@\n  Values[fvars];\nvectorGradientP = Factor[(D[vectorInvariant, #] /. \
bpsRules)] & /@ p;\nvectorValuePass = TrueQ[vectorValue === \
0];\nvectorFirstVariationPass = TrueQ[\n  And @@ (PossibleZeroQ /@ \
Join[vectorGradientF, vectorGradientP])];\n\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- \
*)\nvectorChecks=<|\"VectorInvariantValueZero\"->vectorValuePass,\"VectorInva\
riantFirstVariationZero\"->vectorFirstVariationPass|>; vectorChecks"], 
   "Input"], Cell["Expected exact output:", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData["<|\"VectorInvariantValueZero\" -> True, \
\"VectorInvariantFirstVariationZero\" -> True|>"], "Output"], 
  Cell["3. Raw Kaluza--Klein/Weyl dictionary", "Section"], 
  Cell["Before higher-derivative field redefinitions, reduction of the \
ten-dimensional string-frame metric and the ordinary five-dimensional Weyl \
rescaling give the STU Einstein-frame warp factors and scalars.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData["e2phi5 = z0/Sqrt[zp zm];\nweylFactor = e2phi5^(-2/3); (* \
g_E=e^(-4 phi5/3) g_string *)\ntimeCoefficient = PowerExpand[weylFactor/(zp \
zm)];\nbaseCoefficient = PowerExpand[weylFactor z0];\nmetricMapPass = \
TrueQ[\n  Simplify[timeCoefficient == (zp zm z0)^(-2/3),\n    Assumptions -> \
{zp > 0, zm > 0, z0 > 0}] &&\n  Simplify[baseCoefficient == (zp zm \
z0)^(1/3),\n    Assumptions -> {zp > 0, zm > 0, z0 > 0}]];\n\nsigma5 = \
Log[zp/zm]/2;\nphi5 = Log[e2phi5]/2;\nx1 = PowerExpand[Exp[2 phi5/3 - \
sigma5]];\nx2 = PowerExpand[Exp[2 phi5/3 + sigma5]];\nx3 = PowerExpand[Exp[-4 \
phi5/3]];\nscalarMapPass = TrueQ[\n  FullSimplify[{x1, x2, x3} ==\n    {(zp \
zm z0)^(1/3)/zp, (zp zm z0)^(1/3)/zm,\n      (zp zm z0)^(1/3)/z0},\n    \
Assumptions -> {zp > 0, zm > 0, z0 > 0}]];\n\n(* \
---------------------------------------------------------------------- \
*)\nmapChecks=<|\"RawEinsteinMetricMap\"->metricMapPass,\"RawSTUScalarMap\"->\
scalarMapPass|>; mapChecks"], "Input"], Cell["Expected exact output:", 
   "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[
    "<|\"RawEinsteinMetricMap\" -> True, \"RawSTUScalarMap\" -> True|>"], 
   "Output"], Cell["4. Exact audit of arXiv:2606.31987 Eq. (3.31)", 
   "Section"], Cell["The correction profiles f0, fW, and fPlus are \
substituted into the two Bianchi ODEs and the Einstein ODE. The correct \
angular function is W=a/(2 r^2)+alphaPrime fW. The printed extra constant 1 \
conflicts with the paper's own ansatz and asymptotic boundary condition and \
is therefore treated as a source typo.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData["f0[r_] := q0^2/(r^2 (r^2 + q0)^2);\nfW[r_] := a q0/(r^2 (r^2 \
+ q0)^2);\nfPlus[r_] := -2/(r^2 (r^2 + q0) (r^2 + qm)) *\n  (qp qm - 2 \
a^2/(r^2 + q0));\nassumptions = {r > 0, q0 > 0, qm > 0};\nbianchi0Residual = \
FullSimplify[\n  D[f0[r], {r, 2}] + 3/r D[f0[r], r] -\n    24 q0^2/(r^2 + \
q0)^4, Assumptions -> assumptions];\nbianchiWResidual = FullSimplify[\n  -r \
(r^2 + qm) D[fW[r], {r, 2}] -\n    (r^2 + 3 qm) D[fW[r], r] + 4 r fW[r] +\n   \
 8 a q0 r (q0 + 3 qm + 4 r^2)/(r^2 + q0)^4,\n  Assumptions -> \
assumptions];\neinsteinRhs =\n  -16 qm qp r^3 (q0^2 + q0 qm + qm^2 +\n      3 \
(q0 + qm) r^2 + 3 r^4)/\n    ((q0 + r^2)^3 (qm + r^2)^3) +\n   32 a^2 r^3 \
(q0^2 + 2 q0 qm + 3 qm^2 +\n      4 (q0 + 2 qm) r^2 + 6 r^4)/\n    ((q0 + \
r^2)^4 (qm + r^2)^3);\neinsteinPlusResidual = FullSimplify[\n  D[r^3 \
D[fPlus[r], r], r] - einsteinRhs,\n  Assumptions -> \
assumptions];\nprofileODEPass = TrueQ[\n  {bianchi0Residual, \
bianchiWResidual, einsteinPlusResidual} === {0, 0, 0}];\nprofileNoTailPass = \
TrueQ[FullSimplify[{\n    Limit[r^2 f0[r], r -> Infinity],\n    Limit[r^2 \
fW[r], r -> Infinity],\n    Limit[r^2 fPlus[r], r -> Infinity]},\n   \
Assumptions -> {q0 > 0, qm > 0}] === {0, 0, 0}];\n\nwCorrect[r_] := a/(2 r^2) \
+ alpha fW[r];\nwPrinted[r_] := 1 + a/(2 r^2) + alpha fW[r];\nwTypoPass = \
TrueQ[\n  Limit[wCorrect[r], r -> Infinity] === 0 &&\n  Limit[r^2 \
wCorrect[r], r -> Infinity] === a/2 &&\n  Limit[wPrinted[r], r -> Infinity] \
=== \
1];\nrotationDegrees={Exponent[Numerator[Together[f0[r]]],a],Exponent[Numerat\
or[Together[fW[r]]],a],Exponent[Numerator[Together[fPlus[r]]],a]}; \
eq331Details=<|\"BianchiZ0Residual\"->bianchi0Residual,\"BianchiWResidual\"->\
bianchiWResidual,\"EinsteinZPlusResidual\"->einsteinPlusResidual,\"ScaledInfi\
nityLimits\"->{Limit[r^2 f0[r],r->Infinity],Limit[r^2 \
fW[r],r->Infinity],Limit[r^2 \
fPlus[r],r->Infinity]},\"RotationDegreesInF0FWFPlus\"->rotationDegrees,\"Corr\
ectedWBoundaryData\"->{Limit[wCorrect[r],r->Infinity],Limit[r^2 \
wCorrect[r],r->Infinity]},\"PrintedWInfinityLimit\"->Limit[wPrinted[r],r->Inf\
inity],\"Eq331ProfileODEs\"->profileODEPass,\"Eq331NoChargeRotationTail\"->pr\
ofileNoTailPass,\"Eq331PrintedWConstantIsTypo\"->wTypoPass|>; eq331Details"], 
   "Input"], Cell["Expected exact output:", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData["<|\"BianchiZ0Residual\" -> 0, \"BianchiWResidual\" -> 0, \
\"EinsteinZPlusResidual\" -> 0, \"ScaledInfinityLimits\" -> {0, 0, 0}, \
\"RotationDegreesInF0FWFPlus\" -> {0, 1, 2}, \"CorrectedWBoundaryData\" -> \
{0, a/2}, \"PrintedWInfinityLimit\" -> 1, \"Eq331ProfileODEs\" -> True, \
\"Eq331NoChargeRotationTail\" -> True, \"Eq331PrintedWConstantIsTypo\" -> \
True|>"], "Output"], Cell["5. Complete exact/conditional ledger", "Section"], 
  Cell[BoxData["checks = <|\n  \"DressedFieldIdentityExactInTheta\" -> \
dressedIdentityPass,\n  \"DThetaCancels\" -> dThetaCancellation,\n  \
\"LocalBPSRelation\" -> bpsRelationPass,\n  \"VectorInvariantValueZero\" -> \
vectorValuePass,\n  \"VectorInvariantFirstVariationZero\" -> \
vectorFirstVariationPass,\n  \"RawEinsteinMetricMap\" -> metricMapPass,\n  \
\"RawSTUScalarMap\" -> scalarMapPass,\n  \"Eq331ProfileODEs\" -> \
profileODEPass,\n  \"Eq331NoChargeRotationTail\" -> profileNoTailPass,\n  \
\"Eq331PrintedWConstantIsTypo\" -> wTypoPass\n  |>;\n\nreport = <|\n  \
\"Checks\" -> checks,\n  \"AllChecksTrue\" -> TrueQ[And @@ Values[checks]],\n \
 \"SourceConventionParameterDictionary\" ->\n    {q1 -> qp, q2 -> qm, q3 -> \
q0, jrot -> a, x -> r^2},\n  \
\"CassaniCouplingChoiceForHeteroticGravityInvariant\" ->\n    {lambda1 -> 0, \
lambda2 -> 0, lambda3 -> alphaPrime/8},\n  \"ExactClaim\" ->\n    \"The \
heterotic-minus-standard-Weyl vector-invariant source vanishes on the \
rotating two-derivative BPS background, without expanding Theta or j.\",\n  \
\"ConditionalClaim\" ->\n    \"Field-by-field equality of corrected solutions \
requires the unperformed rotating higher-derivative 10D-to-5D reduction, \
dualization, and field redefinitions.\"\n  \
|>;\nexpectedChecks=<|\"DressedFieldIdentityExactInTheta\" -> True, \
\"DThetaCancels\" -> True, \"LocalBPSRelation\" -> True, \
\"VectorInvariantValueZero\" -> True, \"VectorInvariantFirstVariationZero\" \
-> True, \"RawEinsteinMetricMap\" -> True, \"RawSTUScalarMap\" -> True, \
\"Eq331ProfileODEs\" -> True, \"Eq331NoChargeRotationTail\" -> True, \
\"Eq331PrintedWConstantIsTypo\" -> True|>; \
lagrangianLedger=<|\"ProjectInvariant\"->\"single independent Cassani \
standard-Weyl lambda3 invariant in the Riemann \
frame\",\"IndependentCouplings\"->{lambda1,lambda2,lambda3},\"HeteroticGravit\
yChoice\"->{lambda1->0,lambda2->0,lambda3->alphaPrime/8},\"ExtraVectorInvaria\
nts\"->\"two curvature-free invariants; value and first variation vanish on \
rotating BPS\",\"OnlyConditionalItem\"->\"complete corrected 10D-to-5D \
field-by-field map\"|>; \
<|\"Checks\"->checks,\"AllChecksTrue\"->report[\"AllChecksTrue\"],\"Lagrangia\
nLedger\"->lagrangianLedger|>"], "Input"], Cell["Expected ten named checks:", 
   "Text"], Cell[BoxData["<|\"DressedFieldIdentityExactInTheta\" -> True, \
\"DThetaCancels\" -> True, \"LocalBPSRelation\" -> True, \
\"VectorInvariantValueZero\" -> True, \"VectorInvariantFirstVariationZero\" \
-> True, \"RawEinsteinMetricMap\" -> True, \"RawSTUScalarMap\" -> True, \
\"Eq331ProfileODEs\" -> True, \"Eq331NoChargeRotationTail\" -> True, \
\"Eq331PrintedWConstantIsTypo\" -> True|>"], "Output"], 
  Cell[BoxData["notebook16FinalPass=TrueQ[checks===expectedChecks&&report[\"A\
llChecksTrue\"]]; notebook16FinalPass"], "Input"], 
  Cell["Expected exact final output:", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output"], Cell["6. Claim boundary", "Section"], 
  Cell["Exact: the project action is the independent Cassani lambda3 \
standard-Weyl invariant in the stated Riemann frame; the heterotic \
gravitational normalization selects lambda3=alphaPrime/8; the two extra \
vector invariants have zero source on rotating BPS; and the corrected Eq. \
(3.31) profiles solve the displayed ten-dimensional ODEs with no asymptotic \
charge or rotation tail. Conditional: identifying each corrected \
ten-dimensional string-frame field with the package's five-dimensional \
Einstein/Riemann-frame field requires the rotating higher-derivative \
reduction, corrected dualization, field redefinitions, and radial-gauge map."\
, "Text"]}, WindowTitle -> "Cassani and heterotic matching ledger", 
 StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"]
